Lab 20: End-to-End Integration Project with Apache Camel
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Design and implement a multi-route integration solution using Apache Camel and Spring Boot
Connect a REST API front end to a PostgreSQL database and an ActiveMQ message queue
Consume an external HTTP API from a Camel route using externalized configuration
Implement centralized logging routes for success and error handling across an integration flow
Test and validate a complete order-processing workflow end to end
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Java programming concepts
Familiarity with REST API principles
Basic knowledge of SQL databases
Understanding of messaging concepts (queues, topics)
Experience with Maven build tool
Basic Linux command line skills
Note: This lab is intended for an isolated, self-owned practice environment (a personal cloud VM or local machine). All systems used (PostgreSQL, ActiveMQ, and a mock HTTP API) are launched locally via Docker Compose for defensive, educational purposes only.

The environment should have the following available. Install any that are missing:

java -version
mvn -version
docker --version
docker compose version
If Docker Compose is not available as a plugin, install the standalone docker-compose binary for your distribution, or use docker compose (space, not hyphen) if using a recent Docker Engine.

Lab Environment Setup
Your machine should have:

OpenJDK 11
Apache Maven 3.8+
Docker and Docker Compose
A text editor or VS Code with Java extensions
